From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:05:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add the CTS/RTS pins to uart14

uart14 carries the Bluetooth HCI link on SM8750 boards, and the QCA
driver runs it with hardware flow control. sm8750.dtsi defines the
qup_uart14_cts_rts pin group but leaves it out of the default state,
so CTS and RTS (gpio24/25) are never muxed and the 3.2 Mbaud link runs
without flow control.

Add the group to the default state, as sm8550.dtsi and sm8650.dtsi do.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index d6e0232ed..db119e300 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -1159,7 +1159,7 @@ &clk_virt SLAVE_QUP_CORE_2 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>,
 				interconnect-names = "qup-core",
 						     "qup-config";
 
-				pinctrl-0 = <&qup_uart14_default>;
+				pinctrl-0 = <&qup_uart14_default>, <&qup_uart14_cts_rts>;
 				pinctrl-names = "default";
 
 				status = "disabled";
-- 
2.56.0

